    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d681">

                <pb facs="0657" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/505: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-11T20:00:00+08:00">February 11, 1938—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 11—6:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>244. Reference your 129, February 9, 8 p.m.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d681-f1"/>
                    Hall-Patch, Financial Adviser, British Embassy, told me yesterday afternoon he
                    has definite information from officer of Japanese Consulate General with whom he
                    discussed matter several days ago that the Japanese have <pb facs="0658" n="654"
                        xml:id="pg654"/> intention of decreasing Shanghai quotas for foreign loan
                    and indemnity services <hi rendition="#italic">pari passu</hi> with decrease in
                    revenue. I had received no such intimation from the Japanese or from the
                    customs.</p>
                <p>The essence of the press interview given by Matsui is correctly stated in your
                    message. I am telegraphing separately full text.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d681-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>I have no information on other points mentioned.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d681-f1" n="59" xml:id="d681-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram repeated the Department’s No. 51, February 9, 8 p.m., to the
                    Ambassador in Japan, <ref target="#pg650">p. 650</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d681-f2" n="60" xml:id="d681-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 245, February 11, 9 p.m., not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
